# f1 = copy. The guess whether the DataView is as made ended at the call; its rare arm, which calls whatever is found under the name, came back at a join with anything, and the store
# behind the join took a boxed key and any value. A view of numbers converts what is stored, so the store leans on the number that the typed run knows: in a loop it goes along with
# the stretch: the typed run stores a raw number under a raw key, the rare arm keeps the store that converts. The second print runs the rare arm: a text and objects are converted.
